"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bI'm sure that one could get either variant, depending on the preferences of the users.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bI had this notion of two women mutually impregnating one another but... that can only be counterproductive, in terms of the difficulties of having two children simultaneously (at least if they're an actual couple).</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bAnd also... kind of weird... what would even happen to the progenitive Essence there? Would it basically be a mutual exchange in which both women fall pregnant as though they had sex with a mortal? I imagine that some Exalted investigators of the Dragon's blood have brought up the subject as a hypothetical, and scratched their heads at the implication.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209889-bad-artifact-idea?p=1215643#post1215643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they were <i>already</i> in a mood to poison/electrocute/burn their lover to death, <i>why would they do that?</i><br /> <br /> Exalts know what their animas can do, and they can avoid going all-out to not have it flare up.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI could imagine Exalted sometimes flaring their animas without thinking properly when in the throes of strong emotions. In the case of the Dragon Blooded, it might be attributed to the Great Curse in some cases.<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, doing it to the death? That requires bringing your anima to bonfire and then not permitting a companion to get away when it starts hurting them; it would take at least seven minutes to kill them, under the very most ideal circumstances.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can definitely imagine that there are people for whom part of the appeal of having sex with one of the Dragon Blooded would be doing so while immersed in the holy physical sensations of their anima banner, which might be worth the risk of taking some hurt from it. Not to mention those that would be excited by the risk factor, while also working from the understanding that they can call it off the moment it starts incurring significant injury.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll be the first to maintain that the mechanics are not directly analogous in the setting, so nobody is going to be able to directly measure that each minute exposed to anima flux only incurs a 40% chance of being harmed. Still, it seems like an eminently survivable phenomenon, if nobody involved is malicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T21:35:07-07:00","id":1215682,"title":"","content":"I mean if it's a unique experience you're looking for then it's hard to beat the DB using Invisible Street Performer Technique. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:11:52-07:00","id":1215752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209889-bad-artifact-idea?p=1215654#post1215654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bAnd also... kind of weird... what would even happen to the progenitive Essence there? Would it basically be a mutual exchange in which both women fall pregnant as though they had sex with a mortal? I imagine that some Exalted investigators of the Dragon's blood have brought up the subject as a hypothetical, and scratched their heads at the implication.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Why not just treat it as the effect of two progenitive Essence adding up, like any other pairing? I thought that this was already how it worked, even if two male DBs have a baby through a Neomah, the child has the same chance at Exalting as if it had been a male and female DB having a child through conventional impregnation techniques, no?<br /> <br /> So why would this be different?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:21:51-07:00","id":1215755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209889-bad-artifact-idea?p=1215752#post1215752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So why would this be different?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209889-bad-artifact-idea?p=1215654#post1215654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI had this notion of two women mutually impregnating one another .</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator Levi is talking about the expendature of progenitive essense on two simultaneous pregnancies from the same parents. Twin siblings by different mothers if you will.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, I'd anticipate that the expectation for exaltation would be the same as for more ussually begotten twins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:46:56-07:00","id":1215763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209889-bad-artifact-idea?p=1215755#post1215755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isator Levi is talking about the expendature of progenitive essense on two simultaneous pregnancies from the same parents. Twin siblings by different mothers if you will.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, I'd anticipate that the expectation for exaltation would be the same as for more ussually begotten twins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah! D'oh!<br /> <br /> Thats right, two kids at the same time...<br /> <br /> Yeah, treating it like twins would be my call too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:47:53-07:00","id":1215764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209889-bad-artifact-idea?p=1215646#post1215646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends what you mean by that. They may not have a sex subtree but a lot more of their Performance Charms than Solars' are universal, including a LOT of the &quot;Do cool new thing&quot; ones vs. nearly all of Solars' universals being bonuses or mote discounts/refunds. My personal favorite for bedroom use being Tears-From-Stone Eloquence. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe, that is a way to keep your spouse committed to the institution of marriage!<br /> <br /> But yeah, I was talking about a specific section, like Solars got. After all, DBs are presented as very sexual and sexually liberated beings.<br /> <br /> But now that you say this, it made me realize I never thought of the use of Omni-Applicable Charms in the context of of Sex as Performance sub category.<br /> <br /> Now it makes me want even more to find the right table to play my Zenith Lore/Performance Sex Guru Revolutionaire, uniquely combining Apollonian and Dionysian thought, to spark revolutions of extremely skilled, loyal and emotionally invested people, through Penultimate Unity of Form, Oratory Charms, Sex Charms, Hidden Wisdom Bestowal and Legendary Scholar Curriculum.<br /> <br /> After a few weeks of orgies in town, he would leave, and the town would be on it's way to shed the yoke of tyranny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-06-2018, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:09:54-07:00","id":1215771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209889-bad-artifact-idea?p=1215755#post1215755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isator Levi is talking about the expendature of progenitive essense on two simultaneous pregnancies from the same parents. Twin siblings by different mothers if you will.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, I'd anticipate that the expectation for exaltation would be the same as for more ussually begotten twins.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference there is that even when there are twins, presumably only one parent is carrying them.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe normal mechanism of progenitive Essence, as I understand it, is that you've got one receptive individual and one transmitting one, so the Essence only flows in one direction. Even when using a mystical third partner like a neomah that is a recipient of both parents' Essence, it's only going in one direction, just from both parents to a mutual third party.<br /> <br /> \u200bFrom the way it's described, one cannot normally conceive a child without it receiving one's progenitive Essence. Even with twins in the same womb... it's been clarified that even if highly unlikely, it's not impossible for both of them to be Exalted, which suggests that even the leftover one gets a little bit of Essence out of the process.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo if two women impregnate each other simultaneously, which way does their progenitive Essence go? Does it remain in their own bodies to imbue the life that has been implanted in them, or does it flow into what they implant in their partner? Mind, either way there, one is getting the same half share of Essence, I'm just following a silly thought experiment on how the Essence, let's say, fulfils its obligations under such an unusual circumstance. One has two Dragon Blooded at the peak of their Essence become pregnant with children that have the same odds as if both of them were impregnated by mortals.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it even actually does respond by one side retaining and the other transmitting, to maximize the chances, while the other child gets a thin trickle, so that it has the same result as twins.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm mostly just considering this in terms of arguments against going employing such a method anyway; just elucidating on how disadvantageous it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:30:54-07:00","id":1215779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209889-bad-artifact-idea?p=1215764#post1215764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now it makes me want even more to find the right table to play my Zenith Lore/Performance Sex Guru Revolutionaire, uniquely combining Apollonian and Dionysian thought, to spark revolutions of extremely skilled, loyal and emotionally invested people, through Penultimate Unity of Form, Oratory Charms, Sex Charms, Hidden Wisdom Bestowal and Legendary Scholar Curriculum.<br /> <br /> After a few weeks of orgies in town, he would leave, and the town would be on it's way to shed the yoke of tyranny.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least at the general concept level (of &quot;use sex as a tool to inspire people&quot;) that's exactly the Zenith in my own chronicle. I'll probably have to point them towards the build though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:43:00-07:00","id":1215785,"title":"","content":"Basically is the Lore Training Tree, key Charms being Hidden Wisdom Bestowal, which lets you teach stuff while apparently teaching other stuff, Legendary Scholar Curriculum to do it for a bunch of people at the same time and to grant Intimacies you don't hold, and Soul-Light Spreading Discipline to get a Cult while doing it.<br /> <br /> Penultimate Unity of Form, to let the Oratory Charms work through the bacchanalia.<br /> <br /> So while they may seem involved in a mass kama sutra retreat/festival, they are being forged in mind, body and battle for the upheaval on the horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}